# 6.1.scenario.superposition.bounds.stone

## .what

for each survivor, deep-research its **bounds** — the best-case and the worst-case trajectory. this
is the first consequence-package facet: what happens if this scenario is true and goes well, and what
happens if it is true and goes badly. this is a **research stone**: it gathers cited ground truth.

## .inputs

- `5.3.scenario.rerank.redteam.refine.yield.md` — the survivor set (only these earn deep research)

## .do

- gather via the **bhrowser** only — never WebSearch/WebFetch (`rule.require.bhrowser-citations`)
- for each survivor, state the **best-case** bound (self-limited, benign resolution — cite the
  natural history) and the **worst-case** bound (the catastrophic trajectory — cite the mechanism +
  outcome)
- the worst-case bound of a catastrophic branch is what powers the treatment veto in phase 9 — state
  it plainly, with its citation

## .emit

into `6.1.scenario.superposition.bounds.yield.md` — best-case + worst-case bound per survivor, each
cited.

## .accrue

lift every generic, cited fact (natural-history rates, worst-case outcome frequencies, mechanism
facts) into `accrue/inventory.of=<topic>.md`, case-neutral, per `rule.require.accrue-research`.

## .done when

every survivor carries a cited best-case and worst-case bound, and the generic facts are accrued.
